Stabilization pass after the unified terminal (no new features).

Method: read every boundary (cli/tui, model choice and config, local execution, http client and server, scheduler,
session state, engines) for duplicated paths, unbounded buffers, stale state and silent fallbacks; each finding was
reproduced or proven by reading before it was changed.

Fixed
- Chat on Qwen3.5 GPU replayed the whole history every turn (hybrid recurrent state cannot be truncated). Chat and code
  mode now read the history in 64-token slices, take the existing session checkpoint, generate, and return to it
  (cli/src/session/prefill.rs). Where no checkpoint is possible (CPU, low VRAM) the previous behavior is kept.
- Reported reuse counts tokens kept from before the turn; prefill time is included in prompt_forward and prefill
  (caught by tests/chat_reuse.rs).
- Automatic server reuse needs the same model name, a large enough window and no flag the server cannot honor
  (choose::server_fits); otherwise it says why and loads locally.
- Unbounded SSE event buffer in the code client is capped at 4 MiB (code/client.rs).
- Ctrl-C between prefill and generation could end the process instead of cancelling.
- One chat-model check, one config read per launch, one log opener, one slash-command table shared by the piped and
  remote paths. Removed the dead kv_page_payload_bytes.

Evidence
- Qwen3.5-4B-Q8, CUDA, greedy, 4-turn piped chat (load included): before 10.5 s, after 8.8 s, output byte-identical.
- 8-turn chat measured earlier in the pass: 47.4 s before, 15.4 s after, identical greedy output on three
  model/backend combinations.
- tests/chat_reuse.rs: kept-cache replies equal full replays at temperature 0 and 0.7.

Follow-up: closing test gaps before V6/V11
- Found: asking a server for its model (`marin code`, auto reuse on port 8000) had a per-read timeout only, so a
  peer that kept sending bytes, or one long header line, held the launch indefinitely and grew a buffer. The reply is
  now read for at most 1 s (probe) or 5 s (request) in total and at most 4 MiB (code/client.rs `Deadline`).
- tests/server_reuse.rs: a real `marin serve` of another model, and of the same model with a 1024-token window, are
  refused with the reason and the model loads here; a silent, dripping or non-JSON impostor on port 8000 ends in under
  10 s and is never used. tests/launch.rs: the same for `--port`.
- tests/chat_reuse.rs: a cancel that lands while the prompt is read, and one on the first piece of the reply, each
  leave an exact cache record and a next turn identical to a full replay.
- tests/modes_pty.rs: switching model in the real terminal starts the window over and saves the new model; Ctrl-C on a
  long answer prints "cancelled" and the prompt, /status and Ctrl-D still work (this one needs
  MARIN_QWEN3_CHAT_DIR and a release build: `cargo test --release`).
- Live, Qwen3-0.6B CPU server with a 2048 window: `marin code --model Qwen3-0.6B` used it ("using the Marin server on
  port 8000"); `--model Qwen3-1.7B` printed "it runs Qwen3-0.6B, not Qwen3-1.7B" and loaded locally.
